00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.840
And the first story I'm going
to read is just from the book.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:50.620
And then I'm going to
read a new story, which

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.780
is sort of strange
because it's kind

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:54.850
of fragmented and
impressionistic,

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.930
et cetera, et cetera, et cetera.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:05:00.400
And this is just
a real short one.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.295
And this story came about--

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:09.150
it actually came about
from living in Brooklyn.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:12.600
I lived in Brooklyn for--
like I first left New Jersey,

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:15.120
I came and lived in
Brooklyn for a few years.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:18.450
And Brooklyn's a weird
place because just the rate

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.310
it's being gentrified.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:23.010
So I remember when I
moved into my street,

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.320
it was like mad cool.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.360
It was just a nice
street to live in.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.680
It looked like any place else.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:34.560
But then about a year later,
every time somebody moved out

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.590
of their apartment, they would
build a wall down the apartment

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:40.170
and make it to two apartments.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.450
And then our street went
from a normal street

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.710
with young people.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.870
And then I remember
one day we walked out

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:49.560
and we saw kids outside
skateboarding, which

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.810
is the first sign in
New York that you're

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.570
being gentrified when you
see white kids skateboarding.

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:56.320
You know you're
shit out of luck.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.980
So we had to move out
in like six months.

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:01.260
They raised the rent six times.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.050
So it came out of that
experience living in Brooklyn

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:06.420
and from living in these
apartments with really

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.740
thin walls.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:09.900
I had a neighbor.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.990
I had this neighbor,
these Dominican kids.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:17.030
And it was strange because we
knew more about the boyfriend

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:19.340
than the girlfriend did.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:22.062
So they would be
like all lovey dovey.

00:06:22.062 --> 00:06:23.270
We'd see them in the hallway.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:27.020
They'd be smooching and
[SPANISH],, and stuff like that.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:29.180
And then she would
go away on a break.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.060
And the next day my man
would have some girl

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.690
up at his apartment.

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:34.220
And we'd be like, oh, shit.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:38.570
And then two days later
homegirl would come home

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:40.070
and he'd be like, I missed you.

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:41.695
And we could hear it
through the walls.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:48.140
So in honor of my man, I wrote
this story called Boyfriend.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.540
And here it goes.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.100
I should have been careful.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:54.710
I should have been
careful with the weed.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:57.170
Most people it just fucks up.

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:59.870
Me, it makes me sleepwalk.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:03.200
And wouldn't you know, I woke up
in the hallway of our building

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:06.050
feeling like I'd been stepped
on by my high school marching

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:07.250
band.

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:09.440
My ass would have
been there all night

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:11.570
if the folks in
the apartment below

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:14.090
hadn't been having themselves
a big old fight at 3:00

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:15.410
in the morning.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:19.220
I was too fried to move,
at least right away.

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:22.400
Boyfriend was trying
to snake girlfriend

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:24.830
saying he needed his space.

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:27.680
And she was like,
mother fucker, I'll

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:30.560
